<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <div class="intro-body">
        <p class="section-number">01, About This Service</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">We fix laundry machines. We don't pick up laundry.</h2>

        <p>When commercial laundry equipment goes down in an LA building, the calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run split cleanly between washers and dryers. On washers the top failures are a clogged or failed drain pump, a worn motor coupling or belt that kills the spin, and a leaking door boot seal. On dryers it's vent restriction first, roughly 80% of "not heating" calls are a clogged exhaust, not a failed part, then thermal fuses, heating elements, gas igniters, and drive belts. We come to your laundromat, apartment laundry room, hotel, or gym and fix the equipment on-site, same-day across all seven counties, carrying Speed Queen parts on the van. Commercial diagnostic is $120 per machine, applied to the repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>

        <p>Searching for "commercial laundry repair" across Southern California returns a mix of results, laundry pickup and delivery services, linen service companies, and actual equipment repair. We're the last category. When your washers and dryers stop working, we come to your location and fix them.</p>

        <p>Southern California has the highest density of multi-unit apartment buildings in the western US, and each one with a shared laundry room depends on commercial washers and dryers functioning reliably. For property managers across LA's Koreatown/Silver Lake/Echo Park/Westside, OC's Anaheim/Garden Grove/Costa Mesa, Ventura's Thousand Oaks/Oxnard, and the Inland Empire's Rancho Cucamonga/Riverside/Ontario corridors, a down machine means tenant complaints within hours. For laundromat operators, it means immediate coin revenue loss. We understand both contexts and dispatch accordingly across all seven counties, ten service territories total. BHGS #A49573.</p>

        <p>This page covers commercial laundry equipment repair broadly. For deep-dive information on specific equipment, see our dedicated pages:</p>
        <ul style="margin:0 0 18px; padding-left:20px; font-size:1.05rem; color:var(--text); line-height:2;">
          <li><a href="/commercial/washer-repair/" style="color:var(--red); font-weight:600;">Commercial Washer Repair →</a> drain pump, motor coupling, bearings, door lock, all washer brands</li>
          <li><a href="/commercial/" style="color:var(--red); font-weight:600;">Commercial Dryer Repair →</a> heating element, vent cleaning, fire safety, Speed Queen, Huebsch</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="clarity-box">
          <div class="cb-label">📋 What "Commercial Laundry Repair" Means</div>
          <p><strong>We repair:</strong> washers, dryers, stacked washer-dryer units, coin-operated laundry equipment, on-site, same day, at your laundromat or building. <strong>We do not:</strong> pick up laundry, provide linen service, or do off-site washing. If your machines are broken, call <strong>{phone}</strong>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

